# [Doc][KVPP] Correct the P/D node labels in the support matrix

### What this PR does / why we need it?

The support matrix incorrectly described KVPP as decode-only, while the KVPP
guide and startup validation require it to be enabled only on prefill nodes.

- Correct four `KVPP(only D node)` labels in the English support matrix.
- Correct `KVPP(仅 D 节点)` in the Chinese translation.

### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?

No. This is a documentation-only correction; runtime behavior and public APIs
are unchanged.

### How was this patch tested?

```bash
make -f docs/Makefile build
make -f docs/Makefile build-zh

! rg 'KVPP\(only D node\)|KVPP\(仅 D 节点\)' \
  docs/source/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.md \
  docs/source/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.po

rg -n 'KVPP\(仅 P 节点\)' \
  docs/source/zh/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.md

npx --yes markdownlint-cli@0.45.0 -c .markdownlint.yaml \
  docs/source/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.md

python .github/workflows/scripts/check_md_links.py \
  docs/source/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.md --timeout 300

git diff --check
```

The English and Chinese documentation builds completed successfully. The
changed Markdown file passed `markdownlint`; the link checker finished with no
blocking errors and reported zero remote URLs to scan because this page uses
relative links. The English and generated Chinese matrix rows both contain 42
columns, and the generated Chinese page contains `KVPP(仅 P 节点)`.

## Files

- `docs/source/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.md`
- `docs/source/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/user_guide/support_matrix/supported_models.po`
